WEBVTT

00:07.470 --> 00:09.280
I think it's time to blow this scene

00:09.280 --> 00:11.280
Get everybody and their stuff together

00:11.280 --> 00:13.690
Okay, three, two, one let's jam

01:57.360 --> 02:01.240
Nothing lasts forever.
All things must come to an end.

02:01.240 --> 02:03.790
That is the so called way of nature.

02:03.790 --> 02:06.410
It's rather sudden,
but today is the last episode.

02:06.410 --> 02:07.900
So at this time,

02:07.900 --> 02:10.580
I would like to remember all the things
that have happened and think about them.

02:16.340 --> 02:20.340
Collection Blues

02:24.510 --> 02:26.520
I'm starving...

02:29.390 --> 02:31.700
You too?

02:31.700 --> 02:35.150
"Food For Thought"

02:40.910 --> 02:42.740
Food is very important.

02:42.740 --> 02:45.940
After all, you are what you eat.

02:45.940 --> 02:48.680
Suppose there was a human clone of me

02:48.680 --> 02:51.750
and he had never eaten
anything other than hamburgers.

02:51.750 --> 02:54.360
That guy and I would
genetically be the same,

02:54.360 --> 02:56.800
but we would be
completely different people.

02:56.800 --> 03:00.430
The "Hamburger Spike" might be
more short tempered than me...

03:00.430 --> 03:03.640
Or might be the kind of guy
that goes to church on Sundays.

03:03.640 --> 03:05.970
He might be a violent bounty head...

03:05.970 --> 03:10.230
Or a man that irons his
white shirts before wearing them.

03:10.230 --> 03:14.560
At any rate, the "Hamburger Spike"
is a different person than me.

03:14.560 --> 03:18.680
So in other words,
when choosing your food,

03:18.680 --> 03:20.990
you have to think about it carefully.

03:20.990 --> 03:25.070
I'll have the boiled lobster miso.

03:25.070 --> 03:26.450
Very well.

03:26.490 --> 03:30.000
"Fools Gold"

03:30.620 --> 03:34.290
There's a lot to bonsai.
It's not as easy as just cutting.

03:34.290 --> 03:40.300
Each bonsai has it's own personality...
and you have to let those live.

03:40.300 --> 03:44.970
A foolish person will try to cut anything
and everything off just the same...

03:44.970 --> 03:49.020
They just cut, and cut, and cut
the parts that stick out.

03:49.020 --> 03:53.650
Yet those parts that stick out are
it's personality...and it's originality.

03:53.650 --> 03:57.520
People who can't even figure that out,
don't have the right to hold scissors.

03:57.520 --> 04:01.360
I feel sorry for the bonsai.

04:01.360 --> 04:03.700
Do you know the basics of combat?

04:11.500 --> 04:15.000
"Que Sera Sera"

04:16.460 --> 04:19.460
I hate men with no thought.

04:19.460 --> 04:23.420
But I hate men who force
their thought on others even more.

04:23.420 --> 04:26.300
I hate men with pyorrhea too.

04:26.300 --> 04:29.310
You can't even kiss a man
if his breath is bad.

04:30.770 --> 04:33.560
I love dangerous men.

04:33.560 --> 04:36.690
But...I have to think about the
ones that are too dangerous.

04:37.900 --> 04:41.190
I hate weak men.

04:41.190 --> 04:45.280
I love men who know
their own weakness.

04:45.280 --> 04:48.700
I love optimistic men.

04:48.700 --> 04:50.420
I can't imagine trying to predict what happens

04:50.420 --> 04:53.220
in advance and then living pessimistically...

04:54.540 --> 05:01.250
Life, probably,no matter how it falls
turns out as it's going to turn out.

05:01.250 --> 05:03.920
Yeah, because Ed is Ed.

05:03.970 --> 05:07.430
"You Can't Always Get What You Want"

05:18.150 --> 05:19.400
This is Ed.

05:19.400 --> 05:21.730
Space is very vast.

05:21.730 --> 05:25.610
Ed is traveling to find the truth of space.

05:25.610 --> 05:28.780
When I walk barefoot,
it feels electric.

05:28.780 --> 05:33.700
The network sea is so spacious,
that there are lots of fish.

05:33.700 --> 05:37.920
When I put something
on my head, I get excited.

05:37.920 --> 05:40.670
When I think there is a truth
and look for it, I can't find it...

05:40.670 --> 05:44.170
But when I don't think there
is a truth, I can't find it either.

05:44.170 --> 05:49.890
I can't get a hold of what I want,
but I did get a hold of what I need.

05:51.860 --> 05:53.640
You're too reliant on your eyes.

05:53.640 --> 05:55.140
You're not a chameleon!

05:55.140 --> 05:56.810
You can't see everything!

05:56.810 --> 06:00.310
"Key of Life"

06:00.940 --> 06:03.690
Humans live by their heart's beat.

06:03.690 --> 06:06.490
A beat is a systematic repetition.

06:06.490 --> 06:08.200
In other words, rhythm.

06:08.200 --> 06:11.950
That's right. Whatever you are doing,
rhythm is of the most importance.

06:11.950 --> 06:12.990
When walking...

06:12.990 --> 06:14.160
When fighting...

06:14.160 --> 06:15.370
When eating...

06:15.370 --> 06:16.540
When making love...

06:16.540 --> 06:17.830
When talking...

06:17.830 --> 06:20.080
Rhythm is essential.

06:20.080 --> 06:23.590
"Doggy Dog World"

06:24.460 --> 06:25.710
Hey Ein.

06:25.710 --> 06:27.340
Hey, hey, Ein.

06:27.340 --> 06:29.720
Why are you so furry?

06:29.720 --> 06:33.890
I know! Because
you're sensitive to the cold!

06:33.890 --> 06:35.060
Hey Ein.

06:35.060 --> 06:36.640
In the first place, Ein.

06:36.640 --> 06:39.440
Why aren't you laughing?

06:39.440 --> 06:42.810
Oh, that is because you're nihilistic.

06:42.810 --> 06:45.650
Hey Ein.
After all, Ein.

06:45.650 --> 06:48.530
Why are you so happy?

06:48.530 --> 06:53.990
That's right. Because
Ed is happy, right?

06:53.990 --> 06:55.900
Charlie said,

06:55.900 --> 06:58.160
"A hand must be a hand
in order for it to be washed."

06:58.160 --> 07:01.080
"If you plan on taking, first give."

07:01.080 --> 07:02.960
Now what does that mean?

07:02.960 --> 07:06.250
Isn't Charlie saying, "Do it?"

07:06.250 --> 07:08.050
Right?

07:08.050 --> 07:11.300
You think Charlie Parker
would quote Goethe's aphorism?

07:11.300 --> 07:14.850
"Walk This Way"

07:15.430 --> 07:20.740
"The greatest respect
that a writer can give their readers..."

07:20.740 --> 07:24.360
"... is to not write
anything that they expect."

07:24.360 --> 07:26.360
That's what Goethe said.

07:26.360 --> 07:28.360
He also said this:

07:28.360 --> 07:30.900
"Whether it's a human work,
or a natural work..."

07:30.900 --> 07:37.990
"...what we have to pay special
attention to is its original intent."

07:37.990 --> 07:41.000
That guy says some good things...

07:41.000 --> 07:43.120
Who would have thought that I would

07:43.120 --> 07:46.170
quit being a cop and
become a bounty hunter?

07:46.170 --> 07:48.660
All my old friends are surprised...

07:48.660 --> 07:51.970
Saying, "You totally
betrayed my expectations."

07:51.970 --> 07:52.760
But that's fine.

07:52.760 --> 07:56.390
I want to do something that
nobody else would think of.

07:56.390 --> 08:00.270
Seeing things you've never seen...
Hearing stories you've never heard...

08:00.270 --> 08:04.650
My comrades enjoy that quite a bit.

08:04.650 --> 08:08.150
"A Natural Woman"

08:08.860 --> 08:10.990
I hate simplicity.

08:10.990 --> 08:13.780
I hate overcleanliness too

08:13.780 --> 08:15.500
Being at least a little dirty,

08:15.510 --> 08:19.290
makes your room and
the world easier to live in.

08:19.290 --> 08:21.540
They say that "White
skin hides seven blemishes,"

08:21.540 --> 08:23.790
but I hate hiding.

08:23.790 --> 08:24.870
Stains...

08:24.870 --> 08:26.380
Freckles...

08:26.380 --> 08:27.790
What's wrong with that?

08:27.790 --> 08:30.420
If everyone had the
same skin, same face...

08:30.420 --> 08:33.890
you couldn't tell who you were.

08:33.890 --> 08:36.760
I don't know myself as it is.

08:36.760 --> 08:41.220
That's why...
I can't erase the clues.

08:41.220 --> 08:44.640
They're all guideposts to myself, you see.

08:44.640 --> 08:47.230
Because you can't tell
women from their looks...

08:48.940 --> 08:52.440
"Instant Karma!"

08:54.950 --> 08:56.990
Laughing Bull spoke:

08:56.990 --> 09:01.160
"Swimming bird, do you know
what your body is made from?"

09:01.160 --> 09:02.370
I spoke:

09:02.370 --> 09:03.800
"I don't know."

09:03.800 --> 09:07.170
"Probably some bird droppings
that's rolling around somewhere."

09:07.170 --> 09:08.500
Bull spoke:

09:08.500 --> 09:12.800
"Swimming bird, do you know
what your soul is made from?"

09:12.800 --> 09:14.050
I spoke:

09:14.050 --> 09:15.360
"I don't know."

09:15.350 --> 09:18.640
"Probably some cotton dust
that's rolling around somewhere."

09:18.640 --> 09:20.050
Bull spoke:

09:20.050 --> 09:23.060
"That answer is wrong; yet right."

09:23.060 --> 09:28.270
"Your body is connected with
the universe; yet it is not."

09:28.270 --> 09:33.230
"Your soul includes the entire
universe; yet it does not."

09:33.230 --> 09:36.740
"That is for me...
and for everyone."

09:36.740 --> 09:40.580
"If you hate someone,
you hate yourself."

09:40.580 --> 09:45.080
"If you love someone,
you love yourself."

09:45.080 --> 09:47.000
I spoke:

09:47.000 --> 09:49.830
"I don't feel anything towards anyone."

09:49.830 --> 09:51.670
Bull spoke:

09:51.670 --> 09:55.550
"That is... the greatest
misfortune on this earth."

10:10.360 --> 10:13.860
"Sugar Mountain"

10:14.770 --> 10:17.030
If you give a baby only sweet things...

10:17.030 --> 10:19.310
They say it'll only
want that and wont

10:19.310 --> 10:22.030
eat the nutritious
foods that are vital.

10:22.030 --> 10:26.040
Things like sugar candy
are the poison after all.

10:26.040 --> 10:28.540
Now, it's not like I'm
only talking about food.

10:28.540 --> 10:31.130
The world is is full of sugar candy.

10:31.130 --> 10:32.870
If you only watch stuff like that,

10:32.870 --> 10:36.130
your brain will rot
and become yogurt.

10:36.210 --> 10:40.220
"Chain of Fools"

10:37.010 --> 10:40.220
Well you see, there's a lot to cooking.

10:40.220 --> 10:42.850
It's not as easy as
just randomly adding flavor.

10:42.850 --> 10:45.130
A foolish person will
put in too much flavor

10:45.130 --> 10:47.460
and make a dish
that you can't tell

10:47.460 --> 10:49.390
whether it's beef or chicken.

10:49.390 --> 10:53.310
Those kind of people...
shouldn't hold a wok.

10:53.310 --> 10:55.440
The original flavor of the ingredients...

10:55.440 --> 10:56.550
In other words...

10:56.550 --> 11:00.570
If it's beef, then you have
to let the originality of the beef live.

11:00.570 --> 11:03.370
Otherwise the beef will be sad.

11:03.780 --> 11:06.160
Those who don't work
have no right to eat.

11:06.160 --> 11:09.710
Get you own food.

11:09.710 --> 11:11.290
I don't count.

11:11.290 --> 11:13.920
Women are great
just by staying alive.

11:14.000 --> 11:17.510
"Do It Yourself"

11:17.630 --> 11:22.180
"Don't rely on others
and do things yourself."

11:22.180 --> 11:24.390
I don't know who taught it to me,

11:24.390 --> 11:27.560
but for some time
I've been believing in that.

11:27.560 --> 11:30.230
It's not that big of a deal though.

11:30.230 --> 11:34.440
I wouldn't want to be relied upon
and not be able to come through.

11:34.440 --> 11:39.990
And even if I did I'll wonder,
"Was it really for their sake?" and such.

11:39.990 --> 11:46.160
In the end...
you have to grab your own luck.

11:46.160 --> 11:51.040
Women will quickly betray you,
but men live by duty.

11:51.040 --> 11:52.620
Duty, huh?

11:52.620 --> 11:55.040
That's what I'd like to believe.

11:55.040 --> 11:58.550
"If 6 Was 9"

12:00.130 --> 12:02.300
Doubting everything that you take on...

12:02.300 --> 12:03.930
That is very important.

12:03.930 --> 12:06.220
Information is only information, after all.

12:06.220 --> 12:09.560
If you think what they say on
TV is the truth, you're gravely mistaken.

12:09.560 --> 12:11.550
Open your own eyes, clear out your ears,

12:11.550 --> 12:14.020
and look and listen to the world...

12:14.020 --> 12:17.070
And think using your own brain.

12:17.070 --> 12:19.280
After you've doubted everything,

12:19.280 --> 12:22.490
there is a possibility of
something real to believe in.

12:22.490 --> 12:23.460
That's right.

12:23.460 --> 12:27.280
To believe in something, doubt everything.

12:27.280 --> 12:30.000
It's not the question of that being hard.

12:30.000 --> 12:31.500
It's impossible!

12:31.500 --> 12:34.870
It's like trying to play baseball
without holding a bat.

12:34.870 --> 12:36.880
Hey, Spike!

12:36.880 --> 12:39.710
That's the kind of thing I like.

12:39.710 --> 12:43.220
"Amazing Grace"

12:44.430 --> 12:46.970
The good part about bounty hunting...

12:46.970 --> 12:48.760
is that there are no rules.

12:48.760 --> 12:50.410
To capture the bounty...

12:50.410 --> 12:54.940
there is no written
"Do This" in existence.

12:54.940 --> 12:56.520
But if you do
whatever you want,

12:56.520 --> 12:58.820
they'll start complaining...

12:58.820 --> 13:01.820
Or get mad and say
that it's against the rules.

13:01.820 --> 13:06.410
They're supposed to be living
by following this world's rules...

13:06.410 --> 13:09.950
But who made those rules?

13:09.950 --> 13:13.790
It's not like we were born to obey somebody...

13:13.790 --> 13:17.710
Whether threatened of bribed,
our souls can't be sold.

13:17.710 --> 13:22.300
Unfortunately, the free-lance soul is an antique.

13:22.300 --> 13:24.840
What?
And that heart?

13:24.840 --> 13:28.930
It's too expensive for money to buy.

13:28.930 --> 13:32.810
Lesson, lesson.
If we meet a stranger, follow him!

13:32.810 --> 13:37.980
"My Favorite Things"

13:39.810 --> 13:43.610
Ed has not had any sufferings yet.

13:43.610 --> 13:49.490
Perhaps I might have,
but I don't remember at all.

13:49.490 --> 13:56.000
If you ask why, it's because
I only do things that look fun...

13:56.000 --> 13:58.250
And even with boring things,

13:58.250 --> 14:00.920
I find something a little
fun in them and get excited.

14:00.920 --> 14:05.130
But if it's still boring, I go to sleep.

14:05.130 --> 14:08.510
When I'm asleep,
it's fun rolling around dreaming.

14:08.510 --> 14:09.590
The end.

14:13.390 --> 14:15.890
I didn't put strength anywhere.

14:15.890 --> 14:18.940
I just used your wasted strength.

14:18.940 --> 14:21.810
You have to control the flow of strength.

14:21.810 --> 14:25.200
In order to do that, loosen yourself

14:25.200 --> 14:27.530
so you can counter
any type of movement and...

14:27.530 --> 14:29.110
That's right.

14:29.110 --> 14:31.450
Be like water.

14:31.450 --> 14:34.950
"Unfinished Sympathy"

14:36.040 --> 14:38.580
Bruce Lee was said to say this:

14:38.580 --> 14:41.460
"Empty your mind and throw away..."

14:41.460 --> 14:44.170
"...any form or shape and be like water."

14:44.170 --> 14:47.510
"If you put water in a cup,
the water becomes the cup."

14:47.510 --> 14:51.590
"If you put water in a tea pot,
the water becomes the tea pot."

14:51.590 --> 14:55.640
"Water can flow,
or it can violently crash."

14:55.640 --> 14:59.600
"That is why, my friend, be like water."

15:01.230 --> 15:04.610
As expected, my heart's
mentor speaks differently.

15:04.610 --> 15:07.070
He also said this:

15:07.070 --> 15:09.970
"What I am teaching is not self-defense..."

15:09.970 --> 15:13.200
"...or how to defeat opponents
or anything like that..."

15:13.200 --> 15:19.120
"But rather, how to express
yourself through your movements."

15:19.120 --> 15:23.000
"Whether that is anger,
determination, or whatever."

15:23.000 --> 15:23.890
"In other words..."

15:23.890 --> 15:29.550
"...a method of expression using
the human body with combat."

15:29.550 --> 15:31.640
You can tell that Bruce Lee
wasn't just some movie star

15:31.640 --> 15:35.140
or just some martial artist, can't you?

15:35.750 --> 15:37.520
The chain is long...

15:37.520 --> 15:39.520
Is it the "Way of the Dragon" model?

15:39.520 --> 15:40.810
Oh, you can tell?

15:40.810 --> 15:44.310
"Public Pressure"

15:45.230 --> 15:50.530
If there is a God in this world,
I'd like to ask one wish.

15:50.530 --> 15:55.620
Divine retribution to all
those who take freedom away.

15:55.620 --> 15:59.120
"Whole Lotta Love"

16:00.210 --> 16:01.580
I sometimes think...

16:01.580 --> 16:03.810
I miss out on a
lot with this personality.

16:03.810 --> 16:05.740
I sometimes think so...

16:05.740 --> 16:09.170
that this way all the
good men will run away.

16:09.170 --> 16:13.970
Well, this is who I am
so it can't be helped...

16:13.970 --> 16:16.020
If I act like someone else saying,

16:16.020 --> 16:19.140
"Even though I look like this
I'm really a home maker!"

16:19.140 --> 16:22.310
Or whatever...
Even if it did get anywhere good...

16:22.310 --> 16:24.310
In the end...
hardship...No...

16:24.310 --> 16:27.270
Only regret will come.

16:27.270 --> 16:32.240
Me... It's got to be someone
that will like me for myself.

16:32.240 --> 16:35.870
Well, I think it'll be tough being with me but...

16:35.870 --> 16:40.110
There's probably a man unlucky
enough in the universe though.

16:40.580 --> 16:44.580
Yeah, the blues
harp is great. It's great.

16:44.580 --> 16:47.090
Weren't you a jazz fan?

16:47.090 --> 16:48.480
Don't be stupid!

16:48.480 --> 16:53.340
I was listening to warbling
while I was drinking my mom's milk.

16:53.340 --> 16:55.220
Well you were a clever kid.

16:55.220 --> 16:58.720
"Wild Style"

17:00.270 --> 17:05.810
Over a century ago there was
a sax player called Charlie Parker.

17:05.810 --> 17:10.280
He seemed to be the first man
to play without using sheet music.

17:10.280 --> 17:11.360
In other words,

17:11.360 --> 17:14.230
he was tired of playing the same thing

17:14.230 --> 17:19.240
and started ad-libbing
and playing in his own style.

17:19.240 --> 17:24.250
The music that he started
eventually came to be called Bebop.

17:24.250 --> 17:26.170
That's right.

17:26.170 --> 17:29.750
That's the origin of this ship's name.

17:29.750 --> 17:33.260
"Daydream Believer"

17:35.800 --> 17:41.470
We all sleep while we wake up
and wake up while we sleep.

17:41.470 --> 17:43.600
Is the past reality?

17:43.600 --> 17:46.230
Are memories the truth?

17:46.230 --> 17:49.900
Where are dreams, dreams?

17:49.900 --> 17:53.900
The dreams we dream while asleep...
the drams we dream while awake.

17:53.900 --> 17:56.530
They're both the same.

17:56.530 --> 17:59.740
The people that say they don't
dream only don't remember.

17:59.740 --> 18:03.450
The people with no dreams
have only yet to notice them.

18:03.450 --> 18:05.120
They're cowards.

18:05.120 --> 18:09.420
They want to see them, but they're
merely forcing themselves not to.

18:09.420 --> 18:12.960
"Hang on to Yourself"

18:10.420 --> 18:13.670
And this is just an illusion.

18:13.670 --> 18:15.580
Controlled by an unseen hand,

18:15.580 --> 18:19.010
the truth is still
covered by a thick veil.

18:19.010 --> 18:25.100
But it quietly, like the
moons of Titan, secretly exists.

18:25.100 --> 18:29.850
Eventually showing itself
after the sand storm clears.

18:29.850 --> 18:33.360
"Look Back In Anger"

18:30.900 --> 18:32.420
So...

18:32.420 --> 18:36.650
Let's stop getting angry
over such simple pleasures.

18:36.650 --> 18:40.450
This isn't a joke.
Nor is it fiction.

18:40.450 --> 18:44.700
Or... Have I been
seeing a bad dream?

18:44.700 --> 18:48.210
"Tangled Up In Blue"

18:48.890 --> 18:50.910
A blues man somewhere...

18:50.910 --> 18:54.340
was said to say this after
being asked the definition of blues...

18:54.340 --> 18:56.030
"Blues is..."

18:56.030 --> 18:59.210
"...singing about some kind
of trouble that can't be helped."

18:59.220 --> 19:02.720
"It's All Over Now, Baby Blue"

19:41.630 --> 19:44.600
Sora wo ubaware  Ashita ga ware
The sky is taken. Tomorrow is broken.

19:44.600 --> 19:47.310
Kokoro mushibamu yami ga umare
A darkness that eats into hearts is born.

19:47.310 --> 19:49.810
Yume wa kare  Fuan ni nare
Dreams are withered. All are uneased.

19:49.810 --> 19:53.480
Ah  Sora no yukue wo shiru no wa dare?
Ah, who knows the whereabouts of the sky?

19:53.480 --> 19:55.060
Oshiete okure
Tell me.

19:55.060 --> 19:58.480
Yukiba ushinau tori to kumo to hoshi to ore
The birds, the clouds, and I
lose a place to go.

19:58.480 --> 20:00.780
Ichinichi no sakai ga kie
The borders of the day disappear.

20:00.780 --> 20:04.070
Suteta tokei  Korogaru machi wa grey
Watches are thrown away.
Towns are always grey.

20:04.070 --> 20:05.990
Noboru yane no teppen
Climbed to the top of the roof...

20:05.990 --> 20:08.660
Imagination de hikou kunren
...practiced flying with my imagination.

20:08.660 --> 20:11.410
Nani mo osorezu tobu ore ni miren
Regret the loss of when I flew without fear.

20:11.410 --> 20:14.330
Karada no naka de kodama suru siren
A siren that echos within my body.

20:14.330 --> 20:16.630
Subete nagedashita hito wo mi
Look at the people who gave up everything.

20:16.630 --> 20:20.050
Asu wa waga mi  Miushinaisou na tomi
It may happen to me tomorrow.
Wealth is about to disappear.

20:20.050 --> 20:22.130
Komiageru namida nomi
Keep down the rising tears.

20:22.130 --> 20:26.100
Mou hirakitakunai kono hitomi
Don't want to open these eyes anymore.

20:26.100 --> 20:30.520
Mabuta wo tojita toki ni mieta hikari
The light I saw when I closed my eyelids...

20:30.520 --> 20:35.060
Sagashiteru ore wa hitori  Hitori
I am looking for it alone. Alone.

20:56.500 --> 20:59.460
Usureteyuku shinjitsu no rinkaku
The thinning outlines of truth...

20:59.460 --> 21:02.970
Ikaku shiau fuan to kibou no tatakai wa gokaku
The fight between the threatning
uneasiness and hope is even.

21:02.970 --> 21:05.390
Minukenai Tokyo no sakkaku
The illusion of Tokyo can't be seen through.

21:05.390 --> 21:07.180
Damasarerya shikkaku
If you're fooled, you're lost.

21:07.180 --> 21:09.720
Kono furubita hane wa mukashi mitaku
These old wings like long ago...

21:09.720 --> 21:13.270
Iukoto kikuka mattaku wakarazu kuttaku
...worried and don't know that they'll work.

21:13.270 --> 21:15.770
Demo chuu wo mau yume wa idaku
But I embrace the dream of dancing in the air.

21:15.770 --> 21:18.110
Sono ikikata wa nitaku
That life has two possibilities.

21:18.110 --> 21:21.480
Ah  Sora ga kininari nemurenai
Ah, I'm worried about the sky and can't sleep.

21:21.480 --> 21:23.650
Nemuru furi mo dekinai
I can't even pretend to sleep.

21:23.650 --> 21:26.360
Kore ijou  Hontou no kotoba
Not any more. The real word.

21:26.360 --> 21:29.160
Hito makase ni wa dekinai
I can't leave it up to other people.

21:29.160 --> 21:31.870
Mittsu kazoe miagetara
After I count to three and look up...

21:31.870 --> 21:34.460
Iki ga tomaru you na oozora
A great sky that takes your breath away.

21:34.460 --> 21:36.080
Moto ni modore
Please come back.

21:36.080 --> 21:37.130
Hitotsu
One

21:37.130 --> 21:38.080
Hitotsu, futatsu
One, two

21:38.080 --> 21:38.590
Hitotsu, futatsu, mittsu
One, two, three

21:38.590 --> 21:42.050
Itsu no hi ka ano toki no sora torimodoshi
One day the sky from that time will be taken back.

21:42.050 --> 21:45.170
Mayoeru mono doushi Wa ni nari yodoushi
All those who are lost form a ring all night.

21:45.170 --> 21:47.470
Katariai wasurerarenai
We talk and can't forget.

21:47.470 --> 21:52.100
Utsumuita hibi wo warai tobashitai
We want to laugh off the upside down days.

21:52.100 --> 21:57.100
Umarete hajimete mita senmei na kibou
A vivid hope that I've never seen before.

21:57.100 --> 22:02.690
Sore wa tsuyoi kokoro ni himerareta yabou
That is an ambition hidden in a strong heart.

22:02.690 --> 22:08.030
Mugen ni hirogaru aoi sekai he toubou
Let's run away to the boundless blue world.

22:08.030 --> 22:13.790
Ima, hontou no sora he tobou
Now, let's fly to the real sky.

22:52.250 --> 22:57.680
aishiteta to nageku niwa

22:52.250 --> 22:57.680
Too much time has passed by...

22:57.720 --> 23:04.020
amarinimo toki wa sugite shimatta

22:57.720 --> 23:04.020
...to lament that we were deeply in love.

23:04.060 --> 23:09.720
mada kokoro no hokorobi wo

23:04.060 --> 23:09.720
The wind keeps blowing, while my heart...

23:09.760 --> 23:16.460
iyasenu mama kaze ga fuiteru

23:09.760 --> 23:16.460
...cannot heal all the tears in it.

23:16.500 --> 23:25.710
kawaita hitomi de dareka naite kure

23:16.500 --> 23:25.710
Someone, cry for me with parched eyes.

23:27.310 --> 23:30.720
The real folk blues.

23:30.720 --> 23:39.130
honto no kanashimi ga shiritai dake

23:30.720 --> 23:39.130
I only want to know what true sadness is.

23:39.160 --> 23:46.760
doro no kawa ni tsukatta

23:39.160 --> 23:46.760
Sitting in muddy water...

23:46.800 --> 23:51.260
jinsei mo waruku wa nai

23:46.800 --> 23:51.260
...isn't such a bad life...

23:51.300 --> 24:00.180
ichido kiri de owaru nara

23:51.300 --> 24:00.180
...if it ends after the first time...
